WEBVTT
Kind: captions

00:00:00.448 --> 00:00:04.210 position:63%
These agile animals can
climb down trees headfirst.

00:00:05.258 --> 00:00:08.819 position:63%
To do this, they rotate their
hind feet to point backwards.

00:00:09.944 --> 00:00:12.405 position:63%
These two are digging for grubs or worms.

00:00:13.517 --> 00:00:17.911 position:63%
All raccoons are thought to be
colorblind, but like cats, their

00:00:18.011 --> 00:00:21.632 position:63%
eyes have special reflective tissue
to help them see in the dark.

00:00:28.204 --> 00:00:32.127 position:63%
These raccoon kits have had little
experience fending for themselves.

00:00:32.687 --> 00:00:33.868 position:63%
They are still vulnerable.

00:00:37.962 --> 00:00:40.443 position:63%
And there's an army of
alligators on the prowl.

00:00:41.184 --> 00:00:43.886 position:63%
It's hard to know who is the
hunter and who is the hunted,

00:00:44.146 --> 00:00:46.728 position:63%
but these young raccoons
are tougher than they look.

00:00:47.248 --> 00:00:51.031 position:63%
Another alligator becomes an
item on today's raccoon menu.

00:00:52.692 --> 00:00:55.954 position:63%
Raccoons can measure over
a meter from nose to tail,

00:00:56.375 --> 00:00:58.936 position:63%
and they can happily stay
in the water for hours.

00:01:00.037 --> 00:01:02.619 position:63%
This common raccoon is reluctant to go in.

00:01:03.799 --> 00:01:04.700 position:63%
And for good reason.

00:01:05.981 --> 00:01:08.282 position:63%
The alligator's parents are out and about.

00:01:09.603 --> 00:01:11.244 position:63%
The raccoon has nowhere to go.

00:01:12.765 --> 00:01:15.247 position:63%
The alligators are scanning
the water for a meal.

00:01:17.780 --> 00:01:21.461 position:63%
Raccoons can only swim at about
six or seven kilometers an hour.

00:01:22.301 --> 00:01:25.622 position:63%
Raccoons can live to ten
years old in captivity, but

00:01:25.623 --> 00:01:28.803 position:63%
in the wild they are lucky
to survive for three years.

00:01:31.436 --> 00:01:35.617 position:63%
These delicate little hands are
supremely adapted for finding food.

00:01:37.658 --> 00:01:40.198 position:63%
This family will stay
together until the autumn.

00:01:41.579 --> 00:01:45.280 position:63%
The mother has all summer to
teach her kits how to find food.

00:01:46.785 --> 00:01:49.612 position:63%
And then the young raccoons
will strike out on their own.

00:01:50.374 --> 00:01:53.743 position:63%
Find a den and run their
own raccoon race of life.

